The driver provides support for generic framebuffers that have no
native  driver.  All it needs are some parameters to describe the
framebuffer and an address.  When attaching to a bus  the  driver
is  configured via device properties: Width in pixels.  Height in
pixels.  Line size in bytes.  Bits per pixel.  If true, will  try
to  become  the  system console.  Bus address of the framebuffer.
When attaching to all those parameters  are  retrieved  from  the
firmware.   All  those parameters are configured with Mac OS, and
retrieved from the boot loader.  There is no way  to  change  the
color  map  even when the firmware supports it.  The bus frontend
has only been tested on macppc, i386, and amd64 and requires  ma‐
chine  dependent code to pass the properties mentioned above.  So
far only macppc, i386, and amd64 provides them.
